cartridge "THE THINKERS CABINET/J-F SEHAN & C KOSNIOWSKI/1984"

' THE THINKER'S CABINET - a cartridge of thinking games from two Oric books:
' "L'Oric a l'affiche" (Jean-Francois Sehan, Editions du P.S.I., 1984) and
' "Games to Play on Your Oric-1" (Czes Kosniowski, Shiva, 1983).
' ColecoVision version by Amy & Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py
' from this file (the shell), games/*.alexis (one module per game),
' ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, games/*.pages.txt, art.py, music/*.txt.
'
' THE SHELL: credits, the cabinet's title (carved logo, green felt, stones
' rolling along the shelf, the title tune), the game menu (one blank row
' between lines), the shared font, sound table and music driver (OS7).
' Games: AWARI, TAQUIN, PARITES & MEMORY, SQUARE NIM.
'
' v4, MEGACART 128 KB: the shell lives in the fixed bank ($8000-$BFFF, the
' last 16 KB of the image), each game in its own bank in the $C000 window
' (AWARI 0, TAQUIN 1, PARITES 2, SQUARE NIM 3). build.py compiles the shell
' once per game (shell + that game, a plain cartridge compile) and checks
' that the fixed half comes out byte for byte the same every time:
' - the shell's own data (tiles, sprites, the sound table) are inline asm in
'   never-called subs (fixed bank); the title logo is code;
' - the shell's code ends with a pad to $C000, each game's code with a pad to
'   GameEnd, so the literal pool after it (the shell's strings first) sits at
'   the same address in every bank;
' - no variable has a non-zero initial value (no init table in the pools);
'   the games keep what must survive a visit in the shell's Keep[] bytes;
' - ShellForce uses everything the games use from the runtime, so the
'   runtime part is the same in every compile.

